From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0811: transfer_census_log: the EDRAM ownership transfers by source, destination and reason (with the stencil-bit passes); transfers and resolve clears in copy_byte_census (native stream, zero-copy P2 + P3)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (native stream; design note scratch/zerocopy/DESIGN.md section P2). Written without a build or a
  run: checked with clang++ 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only (the SDK's Release flags) of pipeline/render_target/cache.cpp,
  d3d12/render_target_cache.cpp and vulkan/render_target_cache.cpp (the changed header); 0 errors, no new warning.
  Needs 0810 (copy_census.h). Applies after 0780, and also on top of 0800.
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: At draw scale 2 the EDRAM ownership transfers cost 0.85 ms a frame (24.8 brackets, 153 draws) and nothing logs which they
  are. New cvar transfer_census_log (bool, default false, hot reload; "GPU"): every 10 s `[transfer-census] a frame over N
  frames ...` (transfers made, cut, left out whole by a cut; host Mpx made of the full ones; MB read and written), one line each
  for colour and depth / stencil destinations (with the stencil-bit passes: Direct3D 12 without a pixel-shader stencil reference
  output, the NVIDIA case, makes every depth / stencil transfer as one depth draw, a stencil clear and 8 draws, one a stencil
  bit), and the first 24 rows by bytes: `<source RT> -> <destination RT> (<reason>): made (cut), left out whole, host Mpx, MB read,
  MB written, stencil-bit passes`. Reasons: whole: not a rectangle-list draw / skip_overwritten_transfers is off / the
  depth-stencil target of the tone map draw / a rectangle draw not analysed; cut by skip_overwritten_transfers; colour cut by
  tonemap_transfer_skip; around a clear rectangle draw; around a resolve clear; or the analysis's own reason why a rectangle
  draw keeps its transfers (GetOverwrittenRectangle's reject text). The transfers a cut leaves out whole are counted in
  ChangeOwnership (base class), the ones made in D3D12RenderTargetCache::PerformTransfersAndResolveClears. copy_byte_census (0810)
  gets the transfer read / write and resolve clear classes from the same place. Off = no change (one cvar read a call).
Bucket: REDO

0811-transfer-census.patch (mcla-x86 native stream, zero-copy P2).

